\begin_layout Standard
The VCF
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "VCForig"

\end_inset

 data format (http://www.internationalgenome.org/wiki/Analysis/Variant%20Call%20Fo
rmat/vcf-variant-call-format-version-40/) was originally defined by the
 1000 Genomes Project
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "genomes1000"

\end_inset

 (http://www.internationalgenome.org/home) for data storage.
 The current version of data format can be found at (http://samtools.github.io/hts
-specs/)
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "VCF"

\end_inset

.
 The 
\emph on
Mega2VCF
\emph default
 function serves several purposes.
 It allows VCF format files to be generated for analysis by R programs that
 require VCF input.
 It shows how to extract data provided in the Mega2R data frames for subsequent
 analysis by other R packages.
 Finally, it provides a regression for Mega2R by producing the same files
 from an SQLite database via R code that Mega2 can produce from the identical
 database via C++ code.
 The VCF file and related files calculated both ways should be the same
 except for time stamps.
\end_layout

